Inertial spin dynamics (TSPIN) examples
=======================================

These inputs exercise the tspin styles of the SPIN package, in which the spin
modulus is a dynamical degree of freedom instead of a constraint.  Because the
modulus is free, every spin needs a longitudinal potential of its own; these
decks use fix spring/tspin for that, so that they stand alone without a
TSPIN-compatible magnetic potential.

  in.spin.tspin          bcc iron, NVE, fix nve/tspin.  The conserved quantity
                         is econserve plus the spin kinetic energy, which the
                         thermo keyword ke does not include.

  in.spin.tspin_nvt      the same system under fix nvt/tspin, which drives the
                         lattice and the spins with two independent
                         Nose-Hoover chains at a common target temperature.
                         fix langevin/tspin can be used instead for a
                         stochastic bath.
